./automation/logs/D06-2026-08-08-evening-codex.log-4158-
./automation/logs/D06-2026-08-08-evening-codex.log-4159-**Problem.** SLT-LIFE-02 (d6) targets 'S1 - a live arraysubs-active SLT Daily Core subscription from the SLT-CHK-* run' without naming it, and its arithmetic uses $10.00 day/1, which describes SUB_CORE (slt-core, the control spine). It consumes one cycle by paying it early, replaces both legs and shifts the anniversary. SLT-EML-05 runs on the SAME day (d6) and also consumes one SUB_CORE cycle by setting _auto_renew=off and paying the invoice manually. Two tasks eating the same cycle on the same day makes both results unreadable, and either one silently invalidates the D1-D12 watch's 'SLT Daily Core renews $10.00 unattended every afternoon' baseline that REN-01/REN-02/EML-15/ADM-06 established.
