## SLT attribution decision

A warning line alone has no entity ID and was not attributed in isolation. Raw chronological context in the 2026-08-10 arraysubs-gateway file resolves two warning clusters to SLT records:

- Lines 12, 13, 18, 21, and 24 are five intermediary-event warnings; line 27 records transaction.completed -> payment_succeeded for subscription 12639 and order 12629.
- Lines 67, 70, 74, 77, and 80 are five intermediary-event warnings; line 83 records transaction.completed -> payment_succeeded for subscription 13344 and order 13343.
- The same file provides a non-SLT scope control: lines 88, 92, 96, 97, and 101 show the same warning sequence, while line 104 records successful transaction.completed for subscription 7809/order 7808.

Read-only relationship checks at the cutoff:

| Subscription | Parent order printed by log | Customer | Product | Gateway | Current completed payments |
| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- | ---: |
| 12639 | 12629 | 352 | 12112 (SLT Paddle Daily) | arraysubs_paddle | 6 |
| 13344 | 13343 | 352 | 12608 (SLT Plan Basic) | arraysubs_paddle | 3 |

User 352 is slt-paddle / slt-paddle@example.test / customer. Parent orders 12629 (USD 11.00) and 13343 (USD 5.00) are wc-completed. Completed positive renewal orders also exist on 2026-08-10: 13617 for subscription 12639 and 13605 for subscription 13344.

Conclusion: the "No handler for event" warnings are sufficiently confirmed as SLT-attributable for at least the ten warnings in those two raw-log sequences. The mapped transaction.completed event succeeds, so this is misleading warning-level noise rather than evidence of a lost payment. Finding filed at issues/SLT-IMP-05-paddle-routine-webhooks-logged-as-unhandled-warnings.md.

## Other source findings

